cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RESOLVE: Representation Encoding for Structured Observation Learning with Vector Embeddings"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Colling
    given-names: Gilles
    email: gilles.colling051@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3070-6066"
    affiliation: Department of Botany and Biodiversity Research, University of Vienna, Austria
repository-code: "https://github.com/gcol33/resolve"
url: "https://gillescolling.com/resolve"
abstract: >-
  RESOLVE is an opinionated torch-based package for predicting
  plot-level attributes from species composition, environment,
  and space. It treats species composition as biotic context —
  a rich, structured signal that encodes information about
  plot attributes.
keywords:
  - species composition
  - machine learning
  - ecology
  - vegetation
  - pytorch
  - deep learning
